stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> INIT
    INIT --> INTENT_DETECT: first message passes Input Guard
    INTENT_DETECT --> CLARIFY: confidence 0.40 to 0.70 or ambiguous pair
    INTENT_DETECT --> AUTH_REQUIRED: intent needs higher auth than current
    INTENT_DETECT --> SLOT_FILL: confidence >= 0.70 and required slots missing
    INTENT_DETECT --> RESPOND: informational and all slots present
    INTENT_DETECT --> ESCALATING: trigger fires (human request, safety, fraud)
    INTENT_DETECT --> FAIL_SAFE: confidence < 0.40 counted toward ESC-003
    CLARIFY --> INTENT_DETECT: customer replies
    CLARIFY --> ESCALATING: 2 failed clarifications
    AUTH_REQUIRED --> SLOT_FILL: auth succeeds
    AUTH_REQUIRED --> RESPOND: auth succeeds and no slots needed
    AUTH_REQUIRED --> ESCALATING: 3 failed attempts or fraud signal
    AUTH_REQUIRED --> RESPOND: customer declines, offer public info only
    SLOT_FILL --> SLOT_FILL: more slots needed
    SLOT_FILL --> CONFIRM: action has side effects
    SLOT_FILL --> RESPOND: read-only, slots complete
    CONFIRM --> EXECUTE: explicit yes
    CONFIRM --> RESPOND: no or timeout, action cancelled
    EXECUTE --> RESPOND: tool ok or failed (honest status)
    EXECUTE --> ESCALATING: tool failure on high-risk action
    RESPOND --> INTENT_DETECT: next customer turn
    RESPOND --> CLOSING: issue resolved and customer done
    RESPOND --> ESCALATING: Output Safety block ladder exhausted
    FAIL_SAFE --> CLARIFY: consecutive_low_conf 1 or 2
    FAIL_SAFE --> ESCALATING: consecutive_low_conf >= 3
    ESCALATING --> HANDOFF: package built, queue assigned
    HANDOFF --> CLOSING: human accepted
    CLOSING --> [*]

    note right of INTENT_DETECT
        Any state: 5 min idle expires auth.
        Any state: topic switch pushes the
        current topic onto the topic stack.
    end note
